{"title":"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(modular_congruency/nt_bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (modular congruency/nt bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rational number written in base eight is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/b/77bf65f362bf4da633edc68a7e8c5365d6b21ae2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{ab} . \\underline{cd}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" />, where all digits are nonzero. The same number in base twelve is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/2/c52fac613ec7325863d0ca50ed02a8bc5943e0ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{bb} . \\underline{ba}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"38\" height=\"15\" />. Find the base-ten number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1368cd503da3c6ead8d6c22ce86bc3f002a3ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{abc}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, note that the first two digits will always be a positive number. We will start with base twelve because of its repetition. List all the positive numbers in base eight that have equal tens and ones digits in base 12.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/8/b08ab3a2b0d06458a3cbe035a35d98f718dee038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11_{12}=15_8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/0/bd0437b5be56a90bc36ba3dec8e026dc59627c31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22_{12}=32_8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/74477bb1e1d1e8bab460a0c1ee7c288c19b85f9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33_{12}=47_8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/a/f0a9b461ff5291f2f504b6e6bc25ce485b34a9ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44_{12}=64_8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/5/ef584ba17b1a6dcbc06c1508571381e15d233c6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$55_{12}=101_8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" /> \n</p><p>We stop because we only can have two-digit numbers in base 8 and 101 is not a 2 digit number.\nCompare the ones places to check if they are equal. We find that they are equal if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d65baaf9671227780dd04ab952911036aa5c868.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/a/fda5328bc4703ff88e62aa83ea58ae4e8361f5ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />.\nEvaluating the places to the right side of the decimal point gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/e/e1ee74f0df3c3ccfaf244220511d0f7e7674ddc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22.23_{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/5/4458267b44de068e9186fd0a2df88da0ef542f30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44.46_{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />.\nWhen the numbers are converted into base 8, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/036f83fa0bae6838275cd75fb3b5998c02ee801b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32.14_8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/c/d0c7e0a4371c255c3bdb1af6e5b6e0798266e192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64.30_8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/0/c60b99706378b934d8b19e77a4c7b5f67ef9bbb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d\\neq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />, the first value is correct. Compiling the necessary digits leaves us a final answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/1/d1137064f1887a82783eefb4818756b57ca3b64b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{321}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The parts before and after the decimal points must be equal. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/4/e641203ca37b06b27abcdc6d888b32b7c543ab79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8a + b = 12b + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"129\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/1/fe11fc8efceb9607a9debad8bdad0f5bf465e660.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c/8 + d/64 = b/12 + a/144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"212\" height=\"18\" />.  Simplifying the first equation gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de76f2f17e5b98ef4914da40d1a51e76bb871d44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = (3/2)b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />.  Plugging this into the second equation gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/2/94266e9dd80d7ae4a5b0982365139f7b9bf6c481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3b/32 = c/8 + d/64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"18\" />. Multiplying both sides by 64 gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/b/1fb4604e4ea70e6e557aef3dc4670fc6ec2198ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6b = 8c + d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are both digits between 1 and 7 (they must be a single non-zero digit in base eight) so using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/e/0be94d71d566b29e0f329ad6009b3f4c7b4aaf63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 3/2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d3854ab1db1f4a8d38a5a6ac91e72cd698c12ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b) = (3,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d9cf67e797afa7e029e4b13c4c758197f8cfd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />.  Testing these gives that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d9cf67e797afa7e029e4b13c4c758197f8cfd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> doesn't work, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/8790f46883a296366f038323844601dd2cde9ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/1/35151d50af054df96aaf94e56c1521094d72ac7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 3, b = 2, c = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"140\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9b7a0f00374ac1ac5553a55795b9531d4bdf042.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />.  Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/1/3718dfa4adf7e36c5ae1cd7a7522cc6d615eedd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc = \\boxed{321}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Converting to base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> we get \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfc1701e3d70466c6b7a44760772ab447c841b17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4604a+72c+9d=6960b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"203\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/1/371736bc2c3c9eadd63f4fc08a2552dc6a893875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/beac014240f0733dcb8772a9d08562bbc1862588.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9d$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> are much smaller than the other two terms, dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and approximating we get \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afe79e1583898b1f5f782a3f77e38345c0fc229e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$46a=70b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Writing out the first few values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, the first possible tuple is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/b/96b659ca591d7f7f746e3a378b1f996b1c294af6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=3, b=2, c=1, d=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"18\" /> \n</p><p>and the second possible tuple is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/e/4beb86b9fb81743cbf25dd0893a08edb04fd3fea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=6, b=4, c=3, d=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can not be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/1/d1137064f1887a82783eefb4818756b57ca3b64b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{321}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>By maxamc\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Note: \nAnother way to get the tuples is by setting the different numbers equal to each other.\n</p><p>Doing that we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9940115c75c40c72d10fe98572104c4ce00d79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8a + b + \\frac{c}{8} + \\frac{d}{64} = 12b + b + \\frac{b}{12} + \\frac{a}{144}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"308\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Moving the integer terms to one side we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/8/908aa8f1cdfa300ba28e6b507d82a500397b882d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8a - 12b = \\frac{b}{12} + \\frac{a}{144} - (\\frac{c}{8} + \\frac{d}{64})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"262\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Factoring the LHS:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/e/4fe369ecba1aee152f558236eb2df720ea64440b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(2a - 3b) = \\frac{b}{12} + \\frac{a}{144} - (\\frac{c}{8} + \\frac{d}{64})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"277\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are integers the RHS must also be a Integer and therefore a multiple of 4. However, due to the bounding of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4ba8a5afb5663d7bf609b9c06a2e8d3edcf369f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c, d &lt; 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" /> the RHS must be 0, as it cannot reach 4 or -4.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/c/0dc755b4c3ef0053f482b9079ee37000ba1c5e32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a - 3b = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/007ffe53c38f77efe73f389b2d4f54e3bc9dfe87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a = 3b$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>From here you can bash and find there are only 2 possible tuples.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28modular_congruency.2Fnt_bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(modular_congruency/nt_bash)\">Solution 4 (modular congruency/nt bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (modular congruency/nt bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the problem, we are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd95b6466ba1ab662731fe7c075462004881d321.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8a+b+\\dfrac c8+\\dfrac d{64}=12b+b+\\dfrac b{12}+\\dfrac a{144}.\\]\" width=\"309\" height=\"37\" /> We multiply by the LCM of the denominators, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/8/7080fdbf6e7385fb60b23d885788d3bd7eda12a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$576$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/5/6550f71af48f76b3dd622111ca5dbbcdd92b9ef5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4608a+576b+72c+9d=6912b+576b+48b+4a.\\]\" width=\"410\" height=\"14\" /> We then group like terms and factor to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/9/3a92b2cac2524f6f4606983ee46de5fc88c52151.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4604a+72c+9d=48b(144+1)=145\\cdot48b=24\\cdot290b.\\]\" width=\"442\" height=\"18\" /> \n</p><p>Observe that the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are all divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> must also be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to compensate. (To observe this, one could rearrange the terms to see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/c/b5c6b229a82125633141351b5bcad89c0034db49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9d=24\\cdot290b-4604a-72c=4(6\\cdot290b-1151a-18c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"449\" height=\"20\" />. At this point, it is obvious that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/beac014240f0733dcb8772a9d08562bbc1862588.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9d$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.) Thus, we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/0/3b0e244ea54827f64513ca5a9e3852d8bbbe57d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=4y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> to see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f013416a6d2c21a63bb86c2c290c803990774cd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4604a+72c+9\\cdot4y=24\\cdot290b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"250\" height=\"18\" />. We divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the equation to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/0/8a03ea0e6806cf1a80dbebe7d4e1a3800eb45413.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1151a+18c+9y=6\\cdot290b.\\]\" width=\"218\" height=\"16\" /> \n</p><p>Observe that the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are all divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. By similar reasoning, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/6/776485b0a132cde44ffa957abbe39dd129d30a6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=3x$\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" />. Substituting and dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51d0842bb9a82f3ad301127aac1f8c274c5a8cdf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1151x+6c+3y=2\\cdot290b.\\]\" width=\"210\" height=\"16\" /> We observe that this can no longer be reduced by similar means. \n</p><p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/7/e37a2af6642b77328b7dcc661e68c3f0ac805673.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;a,b,c&lt;8\\implies0&lt;3x,b,4y&lt;8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"288\" height=\"18\" />. We examine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/0/b505733caedc54aef8bf141935876ab2e595fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;4y&lt;8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" />; this becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/a/48a3455280b148d4445addf2d6439aaac5cf7ff4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;y&lt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />. It is apparent that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/8/b980dd1ef77213088ac5d22a6c1fb1614ed46e00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=1\\implies d=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" />. However, the problem does not even ask for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so it may appear that this find is meaningless. However, we substitute our value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/2/d82f4f0928466e722256a22c4570ccba6286829d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1151x+6c+3=580b.\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"14\" /> \n</p><p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/8/478c712c912b457077a3e2bcb642f5100a12bc64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;3x&lt;8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" />. We take our equation modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/e/03e27519b749c40c3b2fc073ecbd68fff5e5cb5a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5x+3\\equiv4b\\pmod{6}\\implies3\\equiv4b+x\\pmod{6}.\\]\" width=\"391\" height=\"18\" /> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/a/eeaac412e513e6d6841f7cba127d8d97f0cd6555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\equiv4b\\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" /> - this is equivalent to saying that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f9982d6194eb1c6fd5ffed96d04552a2e6fdb7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+6n=4b\\implies 1=4b-6n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"236\" height=\"16\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/ace2ffeb7c31ad2a37f4bf0cffb37252bb6cb48e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4b-6n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" /> is always even, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is odd. Thus, this case is not possible, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/f/61f39d0f8d7adc6836a87ef7b056778fdcfbc0f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1\\implies a=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"138\" height=\"14\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />; thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/1/441141806fce48e0008c10b48ea7aeca1dd9d6d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\equiv4b+1\\pmod{6}\\implies2\\equiv4b\\pmod{6}\\implies1\\equiv2b\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"499\" height=\"20\" />. Obviously, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d65baaf9671227780dd04ab952911036aa5c868.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f69c1ec597d19324140f3130e9d63367f4b69c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=5$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> work; however, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f69c1ec597d19324140f3130e9d63367f4b69c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=5$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, then the RHS of our original equation (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/c/8cc83cd5b46026c4a3b6926ff8eddeaaef7c7913.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot290b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />) is much too large to be equal to the LHS (the maximum possible value of the LHS is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/5/9c5af52706a124ca7ee07b8bfa4b711c79931ad6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1151\\cdot1+6\\cdot7+3\\cdot1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"167\" height=\"15\" />, which is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/0/6e0588c55c2d51f1677c8bd4a06da1d49197ce4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1200$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> while the RHS would become <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebcc9974898dfe5c11b98db70065ed4cbea97eed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot290\\cdot5=2900$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"134\" height=\"14\" />), so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d65baaf9671227780dd04ab952911036aa5c868.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>We recall our equation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/4/d04f7e012efcf5f890fe667d4a8b776e935dee4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1151x+6c+3=580b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"178\" height=\"16\" />. Plugging in what we know, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6e4a2d8dfb461c4edb45c2c715f67dae99dd52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1151\\cdot1+6c+3=580\\cdot2\\implies6c=6\\implies c=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"395\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/d/dedb98c4ae8e40fc37d872fcc2d4b2fc0f472bb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{abc}=\\boxed{321}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"90\" height=\"25\" />. \n</p><p>by Technodoggo\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I\" title=\"2017 AIME I\">2017 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2017\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018002630\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.055 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.077 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 644/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1786/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 20190/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.594      1 -total\n 58.80%    7.405      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.75%    4.880      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15488:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018002630 and revision id 285232. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}